WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.036
-You guys, last night
was the Christmas tree lighting

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:03.703 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in Rockefeller Center.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:04.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you see that?
It was beautiful.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.108 size:84% position:42%
And this year's tree
has over 50,000 lights,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
which explains why NBC
just told me

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't use a hair dryer
for the next month.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.180 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I was wondering why.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
But last night was also
the Christmas tree lighting

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the White House.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
And President Trump
gave a speech,

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:20.920 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but right at the start,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
he had some trouble saying
the word "Christmas."

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Listen to this.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Merry Chrissus, Muh--
Everybody.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What?!

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
"M-Merry -- Uh --
[ Speaking gibberish ]

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like they're playing him
in reverse.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.879 line:92%
It's like, "Paul is dead."

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.481
He's like -- Can we play it
again one more time, Dave?

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Merry Chrissus, Muh--
Everybody.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.854
Yeah. He sounds like your uncle
after his third eggnog.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:59.993
He's like, "Uh, Christmas,
and you're the one that said --"

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Trump was like, "Forget it.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's go back to
'happy holidays.'

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.099 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That's much easier."

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.968 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's been a busy 24 hours
for the President.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.407
Last night, Trump flipped on
the Christmas tree lights,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
and today Michael Cohen
flipped on Trump.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's big news. Cohen was
one of Trump's closest allies,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now he's working
with Mueller.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.316 size:84% position:42%
I'm not saying Trump's
running out of friends,

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:26.686 size:81% position:41%
but he today he asked
Rosie O'Donnell if she
wanted to get lunch.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.455 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What? No.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Cohen says
he's cooperating with Mueller

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.496
'cause he wants to put
family and country first.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.997 line:92%
Trump replied, "I totally agree.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:41.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wait. You're talking
about my family, right?"

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.937
This morning, Trump talked
to reporters about Cohen,

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.906
and when he referenced a
document that Cohen once signed,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
he really made
to sure to act out

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.444 size:84% position:42%
what a piece of paper
looks like. Watch this.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He talks about a letter
that he signed.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.481 line:92%
I don't even remember it.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:57.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it specifically talks
about this deal.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:00.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think January,
he was a written statement.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Reporters are like,
"Uh, TV show, uh, three words.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.593 line:92%
Uh, no. Two words? Two words?"

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:11.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Cohen signed --
He signed the paper.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:15.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
He put a stamp on it,
and he put it in the mail.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He mailed it.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.512 line:92%
And then he told everybody..."

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.584
While he called on reporters,
Trump had an interesting way

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:35.855
of using his finger to point
at who he wanted to speak next.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Watch this.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.526 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Reporters shouting ]

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.797 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Reporters shouting ]

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like he's trying
to cast a spell on reporters.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.572 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Like, "Fake Newsicus!

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fake Newsicus.
Really Fake Newsicus."

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.549
It's like everybody's dad using
an iPad for the first time.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.485
He's like, "All right.
Now I just touch it right there.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:09.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to select it.
Here we go."

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.056 line:92%
This is very interesting.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:13.226
I saw that Starbucks is going to
start blocking adult websites

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.061 line:92%
from their Wi-Fi networks.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.096 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience booing ]

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.064 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:21.434
They said there's a time and a
place for that type of behavior,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's all day
at Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, that's...

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.241 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally, health officials
